From 552330a8c1d887ac77fa7f697d5bb37a4184dc1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:17:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show up to 64 textured objects' maps in render mode under
 Vulkan (native GPU plan 5.2b)

render_trace's body moves to the include render_trace.slang. render_trace.comp
keeps the nine named map samplers and its switch for every backend (its .spv
is byte-identical), and render_trace_maps.comp reads every map from one
array with non-uniform indexing. Where Gpu_Caps.texture_arrays holds at least
four objects' maps, render mode uses the array kernel and shows up to 64
textured objects with their maps instead of 3; the Render section's note
gives the limit in force. The array kernel is marked "// vulkan only", so
shaders_msl.py makes no Metal source for it and the build quiets slangc's
profile warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RvkVmjYXFP4g5FN7pGhnXm
